                            <p class="span">
                                Ranking is one of the most important aspects of digital marketing. Where your website ranks on the search engine will directly affect the visibility and success of your website. There are several things to learn about Ranking, this blog will take you through all of the steps in a systematic way so that you can rank your website better on the search engine. Read on to start learning!
                            </p>
                            
                          
                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="1">1. Keywords Are Your Best Friends</h3>
                            <p class="span">Keywords are similar to traffic signs on the road. The search engines use such keywords while they crawl to know what the website content is on. Researching the keywords and adding them creatively will surely give you a good position in ranking your website on the search engine.                    
                                </p>
                            
                                <a href="#"><img src="images/keywords.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="keywords"/></a><br>
                            
                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="2">2. Quality Content Reigns Supreme</h4>
                            <p class="span">Websites and digital media that are high-quality and informative will be preferred over those that are poorly designed and contain low-quality material. More and more visitors read, learn, and enjoy content that is engaging, informative and well-written content.
                            </p>                                                   
                            
                            <h4 class="text-tranf" id="3">3. Backlinks</h4>

                            <p class="span">The way references in the resume of an applicant serve as an endorsement from others, <a href="https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/blog/why-are-toxic-backlinks-harmful-for-website-ranking.aspx">backlinks</a> are the same as well. When a well-known website gives your site link attribution, search engines treat it as a vote of identification. Investigate the different ways you can get quality backlinks by doing guest posting, involving influencers who deal with your niche area, and sharing in online communities that are about your industry.                               
                                 </p>

                                 <a href="#"><img src="images/backlinks.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="backlinks"/></a><br>

                         <h4 class="text-tranf" id="4">4. User Experience Matters</h4>

                        <p class="span">Have you not experienced a situation where you are on a website that took a long time to open or is confusing? It's frustrating, right? Search engines find the sites that are built to cater to user experience on the top menu. Ensure proper implementation of web design principles, site speed optimization, and mobile responsiveness, to avoid customer discomfort in using your website. In the same way, don't forget about intuitive navigation and visible <a href="https://www.kingofdigitalmarketing.com/blog/the-role-of-call-to-action-buttons-in-landing-page-design.aspx">calls to action</a> which are important in ensuring the users' engagement.      
                          </p>
                                
                          <h4 class="text-tranf" id="5">5. Mobile-Friendly is a Must</h4>

                          <p class="span">As more advanced techniques appear the public has a preference for smartphones rather than desktop and PC screens. As a consequence of that, mobile-friendly sites will be ones that will be assigned to the top positions in the search results of search engines. Apply the reasoning of responsive design to the layouts of your website and the coding for devices like desktops and their smaller versions.       
                            </p>

                         <h4 class="text-tranf" id="6">6. Page Speed</h4>

                         <p class="span">Slow loading times kill patience but not when regarding webpages. Several scientific evidences prove that those who have to wait for websites to take more than a few seconds to download will tend to stop using the sites. Learning a way to speed up your site, such as by compressing images, cutting on HTTP requests, and browser caching, is one of the critical areas to look into. Moreover, the use of lazy loading where content gets loaded when it is needed, can give a kick start to page loading speed and increase site effectiveness as well.
                              </p>
                   
                         <h4 class="text-tranf" id="7">7. Social Signals</h4>

                        <p class="span">Social media isn't only about the fruitful memes and the lovable cat videos streaming; it is also a vital tool for promoting online presence. Get to know different media and discover how you can use social channels such as Facebook, Twitter, and Instagram to engage your audience and boost your content reach.
                           </p>
                            
                        <h4 class="text-tranf" id="8">8. On-Page Optimization</h4>

                        <p class="span">This is accomplished by modifying certain factors on the website to heighten the visibility that the search engine will accord. Study factors such as meta tags, headings, and image alt-text that may be used for optimization purposes. These ensure that every page is optimally designed and search engine friendly.
                              </p>

                       <h4 class="text-tranf" id="9">9. Technical SEO: Affecting the World</h4>

                        <p class="span">Though technical SEO might look complicated and intimidating, it is the foundation of all SEO efforts and makes your site more visible and "easily understood" by search engines. The observable factors include XML sitemap and robots. gtm, robotrst. sitemap.xml, and structured tags to build a solid technical SEO structure for the website.
                              </p>

                              <a href="#"><img src="images/New Opportunities Emerge as a Result of SEO.webp" class="img-responsive" alt="SEO"/></a><br>

                    <h4 class="text-tranf" id="10">10. Continuous Learning is Key</h4>

                     <p class="span">The digital environment is always changing, in the footsteps of search engines that keep updating their algorithms. To continue being relevant, know that SEO is a lifetime practice. Read blogs related to the industry, go to the webinars to learn from the speakers, and try different techniques to find out what works for you. Don't forget that SEO is not guaranteed to be every solution. After that, you need to be curious, and flexible and always optimize the strategy for avoiding content ranking drops.</p>

